Subject: [PATCH] lift32: call sites and patched-code variants for run-time code patches

Every direct call carries its site VA (RECOMP_CALL_AT / RECOMP_ICALL_AT, defaulting
to RECOMP_CALL / RECOMP_ICALL) so a port can redirect single call sites at run time.
Lifter(code_variants=...) lifts a host's code patches next to the original
instructions, chosen at run time by RECOMP_CODE_MATCH on the bytes in memory.
patch_sites dwords may sit anywhere in an instruction, not only at its end.

